                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I basically bought this game to pay the developers back for the time I spent playing this game on online ports, but it plays way better as an online game on aggregate sites like coolmath games. The levels are much buggier and less forgiving than online - for example on the intro level \"double back\" where there are 8 sand platforms and you need to use half of them to traverse each side, there is about 2 cm of margin of error online for the final jump - you will almost always overshoot the ledge. Here there is absolutely no margin for error - even holding the left button the whole time you miss the ledge about 20 times before barely getting it. Turning the flash off after death - which is an important accessibility feature for epileptic players! - is impossible in this port where the online version walks you through how to do it first thing. Since it's cheap buy it if you want to support the developers or make sure you have a copy for the next online game disaster - but just play it online if you have the option.",
